# Line endings, scoped to the halves that care.
#
# The Windows half (ime/ core/ engine/ cli/ data/ docs/ drills/ web/ and the
# PowerShell in scripts/) is deliberately NOT covered. It is checked out
# through core.autocrlf=true and its worktree is mixed -- core/composer.cpp
# sits as LF while data/Makefile and docs/spec.md sit as CRLF. A repo-wide
# `* text=auto` would buy nothing there and would change what every one of
# those files looks like after the next checkout.
#
# The macOS half cannot tolerate a CR anywhere: bash dies with
# "$'\r': command not found" on a .command, and clang reports bogus line
# numbers in a .mm.
#
# Never run `git add --renormalize`. It is a no-op today and it is the one
# command that could turn this into a whole-tree diff.

/mac/**             text=auto eol=lf

# Unanchored on purpose, as a net for shell scripts written outside mac/
# (scripts/build-data.sh). Verified safe when added: no .sh or .command
# existed anywhere else in the tree.
*.sh                text eol=lf
*.command           text eol=lf

# A no-op today (pages.yml is already LF both sides); here so a workflow
# authored on Windows can never ship a CR inside a `run: |` block.
/.github/**/*.yml   text eol=lf

# Belt and braces: text=auto already detects these, but a generated icon or
# screenshot landing under mac/ must never be line-ending converted.
/mac/**/*.png       binary
/mac/**/*.tiff      binary
/mac/**/*.icns      binary
